A||||15||Nashco||Preferred Exhuast Tips?||||5||
Z||000000||Nashco||10-19-2001||02:51 AM||||I'm getting my exhaust done tomorrow, and I haven't got any tips yet.  I am just going to use straight pipe, without a catalytic converter, for the moment.  This is basically because there's no checks in Alabama, and I am strapped for cash.  When I get the pipe all bent, I'm just going to have the pipe come out as if there were tips, but not put any on.<P>So, I will be buying the tips and perhaps a cat. con. soon, and I'm curious if anybody has any recommendations.  Have you used some that you really liked, or saw some?  Cost is an issue, and I'm hoping to get something under 50 bucks per side, but still have a quality part.  If you know how much yours were, and where you got them, that'd be bonus information!  Thanks for your opinions <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||10-19-2001||04:18 AM||||I don't know where to get any, but I know what type/style I'll be looking for whenever I need some.  I want some that are oval and just fit in the fascia cut out.  SS with rolled edges.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||10-19-2001||09:07 AM||||I bought mines at Discoutn Autoparts. $40 per side, 3" doubles, chrome. Brand is Bosal Brospeed or something like that. Other than that is SS which is very expensive for a similar tip. You can see them at:<BR> <A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/alexft/Alex4mula/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://community-2.webtv.net/alexft/Alex4mula/index.html</A> <P>Have been there for a year and still look like new. I wax them at least every two weeks with BlueMagic.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||10-19-2001||09:36 AM||||You found a muffler shop that will put an exhaust on without a catalytic converter?  Wow.  That's rare.  Even though you may not have emissions testing in your area, it's still a Federal offense for them to tamper with or remove the cat.  When I was putting the replacement cat on my Formula, the muffler shop misunderstood me, thinking I was taking it off, and wasn't even interested in touching the car until I told him I was putting one on instead of taking one off.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||10-19-2001||09:51 AM||||I personally quite like the Pacesetter Monza Resonator Tips. (I have them in gold, but they are much more commonly seen in Chrome) They can be found at many auto parts stores- and J.C.Whitney carries them also.<P>Check out this thread on my Exhuast for pics & info...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013191.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013191.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fformula88||10-19-2001||10:33 AM||||Whatever you get, don't get the cheepo's!  I've seen way too many cars lately with rusty exhaust tips!  Not good!  I prefer the dual tip look on cars over a single tip, even if its reasonable in size and not a fart can!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  The Grand Am GT's with the dual tip chrome exhaust tips from the factory look good to me... they just need to be a little bigger in diameter!  (not that I would replace them if I had a Grand Am, just if I was buying new!)||||reg||1
Z||000006||Philphine||10-19-2001||12:19 PM||||i put dual dtm's on my coupe that has a gt facia on it. about $80 and $20 to have them put on. they fill in the space pretty compleatly and i like them. and just this week i cut the megaphone part off my gt and put on 4 indiviual tips i got at auto zone. kinda cheap so i am sort of worried about how durable they are but i like how they look. they sort of remind me of supertrapps, just a little. tips and reducer pipes to weld them on (they were really the frankinstein looking bolt on type) about $120. tacked them on myself.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Nashco||10-19-2001||01:32 PM||||Well, I just got it all done.  They didn't have anything going on, so I literally drove up to the shop and parked on the rack.  In and out in about 1.5 hours.  I didn't get to use my flowmaster, as it wouldn't fit as I had anticipated.  I guess I should have asked around and done a little research.<P>Now that I think about it, I do remember (artherd?) somebody mentioning having to section part of the flowmaster to use it on the 88 cradle....doh!<P>Anyway, ended up using a "turbo pipe" that he had.  It looks like a glass pack on the outside, but has fully aluminized insides, and is basically just a baffle of sorts.  He also had a set of dual (split) tips, look basically like the GT tips, except they aren't megaphone style, they're straight.<P>I got a good deal, and it was done quickly, so I'm happy.  I can now CLEARLY hear my exhaust leaks elsewhere.  I don't know how long the tips will last, as they were cheap, but everything else is aluminized.  There's plenty of pipe there, if I want to cut those off and put on some better ones down the road.  Probably won't do that until they get bad rust though, as I'm not too picky about that.<P>With no cat, just the turbo pipe, the sound is alright.  It doesn't have much tone to it; it's just kind of gurgly and resonant.  I'm sure with the flowmaster, especially at idle, the sound would have been much cleaner.  All said and done, I'm just glad it's finally replaced...my old cat was toasted from having raw fuel blow up in it all the time (pipe had holes on both sides of it), and the muffler was separating so bad that you could literally stick two fingers in and touch the inner baffles.<P>Thanks for your recommendations!  Hopefully somebody else will be able to use this info.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||MinnGreenGT||10-19-2001||01:36 PM||||Nashco... you wouldn't happen to know how long (connection to connnection) how long the turbo pipe was- would you? Also an approximate diameter? I'm looking at doing something similiar with a y-pipe cutout (see link above for illustration) and need to find something short that will deaden the sound a lot more than my resonator tips  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||TRL46202||10-19-2001||02:08 PM||||would also like that part # for the "turbo pipe" thanks,<P>Tom||||reg||1
Z||000010||Nashco||10-19-2001||04:00 PM||||The "muffler" itself is approximately 15" long and 4" in diameter.  At each end it has about 3" of 2.25" pipe.  I have NO IDEA of the manufacturer.  If you need more info, I could drive out to the place and get more.  He only charged me 25 bucks for it, so I know it had to be cheaper for him, and he claims it is fully aluminized.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000011||MinnGreenGT||10-19-2001||04:11 PM||||Don't necessarily need to drive do you?  Give him a call though!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
